{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":4967197,"ns":0,"title":"Baer norm","extract":"In mathematics, in the field of group theory, the norm of a group is the intersection of the normalizers of all its subgroups. This is also termed the Baer norm, after Reinhold Baer.","description":"Concept in group theory","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}